  "id": "COMPOUND:20982 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Tenuiphenone B and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with this complex. Tenuiphenone B is linked to WiDr, a cell line that is a target of both Talosin A and Polyphillin C, which in turn target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Similarly, Tenuiphenone B is also linked to Isosalsoline, which also targets the same complex. These findings indicate that Tenuiphenone B may act through a pathway that involves the activation or modulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially through the interaction with its downstream targets. The scores from the different paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role for Tenuiphenone B in influencing the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this hypothesis.",
